   "he": "אָכַל אוֹכָלִין שֶׁאֵין רְאוּיִן לַאֲכִילָה. אָמַר רָבָא: כַּס פִּלְפְּלֵי בְּיוֹמָא דְכִפּוּרֵי — פָּטוּר. כַּס זַנְגְּבִילָא בְּיוֹמָא דְכִפּוּרֵי — פָּטוּר.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: If one «ate food that is» not «fit for eating,» he is exempt. «Rava said:» If «one chews» raw «pepper on Yom Kippur, he is exempt,» since this is not considered eating. Similarly, if «one chews ginger [zangvila] on Yom Kippur, he is exempt.»"
  }
